# Generated artefacts.
#
# Two rules decide what lives here:
#   * anything large and regenerable is ignored;
#   * anything that makes a number TRACEABLE is kept, however small.
#
# Two git details this file depends on:
#   * `dir/*`, not `dir/`. Git will not descend into an excluded directory, so
#     `dir/` makes every negation below it dead.
#   * NO TRAILING COMMENTS. `#` only starts a comment at the start of a line;
#     anywhere else it becomes part of the pattern and the rule matches nothing.

# Run tables are ~6-8 MB each and ARE committed: that makes "which run built
# the universe" answerable by commit hash instead of by a chat message.
runs/*
!runs/.gitkeep
!runs/*.parquet
!runs/*manifest*.json

# The sqlite cache is far too large for git; only its manifest is kept.
cache/*
!cache/.gitkeep
!cache/*manifest*.json

# `real.py` and `analysis.py` write into a SUBDIRECTORY - effects/real,
# analysis/real_<system>_kc<k_c> - so the two negations below are not enough on
# their own. `effects/*` excludes the `effects/real` directory entry, git then
# never descends into it, and `!effects/*manifest*.json` cannot fire on
# anything inside: the same trap this file warns about at the top, one level
# further down. Without `!effects/*/` the manifests for the headline numbers
# are unreachable, which is exactly the traceability the rule exists to keep.
# The parquets and CSVs stay ignored - only the manifests are rescued.
# Three lines per directory, and all three are needed. `!effects/*/` only lets
# git descend; on its own it un-ignores everything inside, parquets included.
# `effects/*/*` excludes the contents again, and the last line rescues the
# manifests alone.
effects/*
!effects/.gitkeep
!effects/*manifest*.json
!effects/*/
effects/*/*
!effects/*/*manifest*.json

analysis/*
!analysis/.gitkeep
!analysis/*manifest*.json
!analysis/*/
analysis/*/*
!analysis/*/*manifest*.json

runs_mock/

data/*.parquet
data/*.frozen
data/queries.tsv
data/qrels.txt

# The query split and the reference subset ARE committed: both are small, both
# are contracts other members depend on, and committing the materialised file
# turns "should be identical" into "is identical". Listed here as a reminder
# that they are deliberately NOT ignored.
#   data/query_split.json
#   data/reference_subset.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
data/.trec_cache/

# LaTeX build artefacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
